Hi Andrew

Once I tried to incorporate a Thin Plate Spline (2D in the plane) as a random effect in TMB but I did not get good results. However, that was only because I did not have a complete understanding with c++. I'm working in my thesis in a low rank approximation for radial basis functions (aka kernel methods) and I'm happy to see someone with similar questions.
My first analysis is with a Normal model like this y = f(s) + e  (Normal errors) and the minimization: ||y - E*\delta - T*\alpha||^2 + \lambda *\delta^T*E*delta (following the GAM book of Simon Wood).
So, your question is related with a low rank approximation of the penalization term? (which in turn is the solution for the null space J_{md}?)

Regards

​
Joaquin Cavieres G.
PhD (c) in Statistics
Institute of Statistics
Universidad de Valparaíso

