My experience with the thin plate shrinkage smoother in 2D has been okay so far with TMB, interesting that you did not have any luck there.  Did you try to fit the usual thin plate or did you do the shrinkage version? When I tried the one with a null space GMRF function complained which makes sense since I cannot evaluate the density if the precision is singular.

Maybe easiest to discuss over actual code.  I've attached some for a simple linear model with simulated data.  These are the two approaches I've tried so far.  I have used the `bs = "ts"` to specify the shrinkage smoother but I've also done this myself for other smoothers such as `bs = "gp"` and `bs = "ds"` using the same approach as Simon Wood implemented for "ts" (so far as I've been able to tell anyway).

I like these low rank smoothers, something like a cubic spline might need many more parameters to achieve a similar degree of flexibility.  That is fine in many cases but I've found TMB can struggle in the model Im using them in (a spatial capture-recapture model that integrates the spline over space - this involves a numerical integration scheme and so I think the graph of the likelihood just gets very big)

Andy

