Ok, I understand. You took the penalized matrices from the fit with mgcv. I was trying create the classical TPS (log^2||r||log) as a function in c++ and then passing it to TMB.  I did that because I wanted to fit a complete model in TMB (not using mgcv) but your approx looks very nice.
Well, I don't remember if you can use a GMRF to approximate any type of matrix (distances in this case) because it gives you a special structure and probably non definite positive, and as you are doing GMRF(Q)(x) then something is happening with your sparse matrix Q (I'm thinking out loud).

There are a lot of methods to factorize a matrix, for example if you want to use a GMRF to approximate a dense matrix then could use a sparse solver (but you will be out of the TMB environment). Is there a lot of ideas to develop but the problem is do it compatible with TMB.

